---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

---
<PageLayout
  title="About | Kanon Tax & Advisory"
  description="Kanon Tax & Advisory is an independent tax and advisory practice in Houston, Texas, run by a licensed CPA with a Big 4 and consulting background."
  h1="Your Trusted Financial Partner"
  eyebrow="About Kanon Tax & Advisory"
  lede="A licensed CPA working directly with a limited number of clients, so you always know who is handling your work."
  crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'About' }]}
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:32px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          As a licensed CPA with experience at leading professional services firms, I founded Kanon
          Tax &amp; Advisory to bring institutional-quality financial guidance directly to individuals
          and small businesses — without the complexity or overhead.
        </p>
        <p>
          My passion is helping people face the often-intimidating world of taxes and finances, gain
          clarity on their financial picture, and build a defined plan for their future. I believe
          everyone deserves a knowledgeable advocate in their corner.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether you're an individual seeking tax preparation and planning, a couple thinking about
          retirement and wealth, or a small business owner navigating growth — I take the time to learn
          about you, your family, and the things that matter most to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Where I tend to help most</h2>
        <p>
          A decade in Big 4 and independent consulting means most of my work has been on the technical
          side — foreign currency, lease and revenue standards, multi-entity consolidations, ERP-era
          ledgers at companies considerably larger than the ones I serve here.
        </p>
        <p>
          Applied at this scale, what that experience is really good for is judgment about which
          problems are worth your attention. Clients often find me in a year when something meaningful
          has happened — equity vesting, a business adding an entity or a state, a change in the family.
          Those are the years where having someone who has seen it before makes the most difference.
        </p>

        <h2>How the practice is set up</h2>
        <p>
          I hold an active CPA license and am authorized to represent taxpayers before the IRS.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not provide attest services.</strong> No audits, reviews, or compilations. If a
          lender or investor requires one, I'll say so directly and help you find a firm that performs
          them.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We are not a registered investment adviser.</strong> I advise on the tax consequences
          of decisions. I don't recommend securities or manage assets. Where you already work with a
          financial adviser, I'd much rather coordinate with them than work around them.
        </p>

        <h2>Working together</h2>
        <p>
          I work with clients across the country, so nothing here requires you to be in Houston.
          Documents move through an encrypted portal rather than email, and most conversations happen by
          video or phone. The first one is free, and it usually tells us both whether this is a good fit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand
    heading="Have a situation worth a conversation?"
    body="If you're not sure whether it's complicated enough to need a CPA, that question is itself a good reason to ask."
  />
</PageLayout>
